  "body": "## Summary\n\nThree smartcopy output defects reported against #77, all reproducible with `ffmpeg`/`ffprobe` and `mediamolder run` on 80-frame 29.97 fps fixtures (GOP 12, two B-frames) cut mid-GOP at both ends:\n\n1. **Cuts from constant-rate B-frame sources had uneven DTS steps** (a 6006-tick jump at the head, a 1 + 2001 pair at a join), which completed-file probes reject as variable frame rate.\n2. **Re-encoded AAC lost the head of the window**: the output started one AAC frame late behind a 21 ms empty edit.\n3. **An `hvc1` HEVC source gave an `hev1` cut**, which AVFoundation does not decode at all.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **DTS.** `sendRun` extrapolates the run's first DTS values one frame at a time from the run's first frame instead of reading the priming GOP, and `emitCopy` retimes a copied keyframe whose leading pictures were re-encoded with the run (its source DTS sits those frames too early). The frame tick and the source reorder depth come from the GOP's own PTS steps rather than the demuxer's average frame rate. The cut tests now assert every DTS step is one frame for H.264 closed/open GOP and HEVC, including the open-GOP cut-position sweep.\n- **AAC.** The auto-inserted `atrim` is followed by `asetpts=PTS-STARTPTS` (unless `copy_ts`), and the sink treats channels fed through an `__atrim__` node as internally trimmed: no ss/to drop or stop, no start shift, only segment re-anchors (minus the rebase). The encoder's priming packet (−1024 samples) and the packet holding the window's first samples now reach the muxer. Both sink loops take the cut compare and the anchor from shared helpers; `-shortest` compares written (post-shift) PTS on every channel.\n- **hvc1.** HEVC config mode: a trial x265's VPS/SPS/PPS are renumbered to ids the source does not use (Exp-Golomb fields rewritten, trailing bits re-padded) and appended to the output hvcC; every re-encoded slice header is renumbered to the new PPS id with its slice data kept byte-aligned. The track keeps the source's sample entry. An hvcC source whose sets cannot be renumbered fails the job rather than falling back to `hev1`; in-band remains only for Annex B sources.\n- Docs (`smartcopy.md`, `json-config-reference.md`) and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `repro.sh` from the report: all three fixtures give `41×1001` DTS steps with no clamps; the AAC cut is `start_time 0`, duration 1.401000, first packets −1024/0, and its decoded samples are identical to the `ffmpeg -af atrim,asetpts -c:a aac` reference (max |diff| 0 over the file); the HEVC cut is `hvc1` and `AVAssetReader` decodes 42/42 frames (the H.264 cut, avcC with two SPS/PPS, decodes 42/42 as well).\n- New tests: constant-DTS assertion in the cut tests; `TestAudioTrimAACKeepsHeadOfWindow` (sine source, unaligned start); `TestHEVCRenumberRoundTrip` on real x265 output (ids read back, slice re-parses, slice data byte-identical) plus `TestLastOneBit`, `TestHvcCWithParamSets`, `TestBitBufUE`; `TestSinkWriter_TrimmedChannelShift` and `TestSinkWriter_TrimmedChannelCutAndShortest` for rotation re-anchoring and `-shortest` on a rebased channel.\n- `go test ./job ./av ./processors ./internal/gui ./cbs/...` pass; `go vet` and `gofmt` clean.\n",
